{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/677037-invocation-theme-bs-s-b-rules","id":677037,"title":"Invocation Theme (BS:S&B rules)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-24T17:18:12-07:00","id":677037,"title":"Invocation Theme (BS:S&B rules)","content":"This is an old draft of notes I had written up for a Vampire chronicle. Seeing the Dragolescu bloodline reminded me of it, so I thought I would share it for comments and suggestions. So, let me have it people!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Invocation</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Practitioners of Cruac point as far back as Homer's epics to demonstrate the true age of this Theme; blood offerings luring the shades of the dead -and other ephemera- out of their ignorant bliss and before the presence of witches. After all, for those who view life, death, and undeath as part of the Natural process, this theme poses a very minute leap in logic. Theban sorcerers, on the other hand, are more likely to draw inspiration from the stories of King Solomon and his practice of the dark arts, warning of the perils awaiting those not of strong faith and adequate preparation. After all, the shades themselves as well as their places of origin constitute pretty much uncharted waters for most blood sorcerers... Worse yet, it is not unheard of practitioners of this Theme to unwittingly invite Strix or other demonic possession into their undead bodies...Therefore, sorcerers are expected to have a strong understanding of <b>at least</b> the Protection and Destruction themes, which coupled with Invocation, allow them to deal with said entities in case they get unruly. And they do get unruly so very often.<br /> <br /> The spell's <b>Area of Effect</b> determines how far will the sorcerer's calling for any kind of entity reach. <b>Number of Targets</b> allows the summoning of a specific number of ephemerals, while <b>Potency</b> helps determine their relative power level. <b>Range</b> is more useful when calling on specific entities, although it applies only to the material and Twilight, and chances are no ephemeral might be around to heed the summoning. Lastly, <b>Duration</b>, apart from limiting the length of the spell's effects, can be coupled with <b>Size</b> to allow travel (and time of return to the Material) to otherwordly realms. The <b>where</b> and the <b>when</b> of that return, however, is hard to predict.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Invocation </b></span></span>\u25cf<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Allows the ritualist to summon, perceive, and command ephemerals in their Twilight state. The sensitivity of mortals to such entities can also be manipulated, as can some minor properties of Wyrm's nests. Thin places between other realms can be vaguely sensed at this level.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Invocation </b></span></span>\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The ritualist is now capable of summoning beings from other realms, commanding them and banishing them (provided she can maintain her concentration long enough). Summoned ephemerals can also be forced inside lifeless corpses, or the soulless victims of the Sons of Phobos. Sensing thin places now becomes accurate, although the realm to which the place is connected still eludes the sorcerer. Ephemerals can be anchored to objects or locations by the ritualist, and other exorcists attempting to banish them suffer a penalty equal to the ritual's Potency.<br /> <br /> Through occult phenomena, like visions and automatic writing, which may or may not carry with them the risk of possession, the ritualist can also peek into alternate realms of existence and may even produce (crude) maps extending to a radius equal to the spell's Area of Effect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Invocation </b></span></span>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The rtiualist now fully perceives other realms (such as the Shadow or the Underworld) at the cost of rendering himself blind in the material. His pupils dilate to the point of covering the entire eye, and he is only vaguely aware of spacial limitations and threats in his physical surroundings (requiring a successful Resolve + Composure roll to notice). Using <i>thin places</i> (whose destination she can now discern), the ritualist can also travel outside the material, although bound by the ritual's finite Duration.<br /> <br /> Ephemerals can also be bound to the sorcerer, turning them into obedient familiars and affecting them with the same effects of other Themes of Blood Sorcery (as if they were material entities). Maps created through a combination of Divination and Invocation are now extremely accurate and can cover a great radius.<br /> <br /> Wyrm's nests can also be completely altered, drawing to them very different sorts of spirits, entities, or magical energies.<br /> <br /> <b>The Crossroads</b>, a realm unique to Kindred ritualists, now becomes accessible to the sorcerer. Each visitor here is welcomed by a unique experience, although a few motifs remain constant for all. Some kind of crossroads, either urban or akin to trails in the wilderness, are populated by people affected throughout the Kindred's existence. Unable to notice the vampire at first, if she stumbles upon them or somehow draws their attention, these shades may attack or (<i>worse</i>) pull her into their own time and place, demanding justice. Rumors and notes written by blood sorcerers who were never heard from again, imply that the Crossroads can be useful for time travel to crucial points in the Kindred's Requiem, although the notes suggest they hadn't succeeded up until the time of writing. Some have even suggested that there's always a secret doorway hidden in the Crossroads, leading to the dark places from where the Strix originate...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Invocation </b></span></span>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Now the ritualist can transfer the effects and applications of this Theme onto objects that can be triggered by anyone (unless otherwise specified). Her vision can be attuned to both an otherwordly realm </span><i>and</i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> the material, and blood magic works even after the Vampire has crossed to one of them. Practitioners of Auspex can also astrally project their consciousness into other realms and even interact with their denizens.<br /> <br /> Ephemerals can now be diablerized, as if they were Kindred. Any Numinas gained through the process are activated at the cost of letting the spirit's echo struggle for control over the diablerist's body. Using the Transmutation Theme can change Essence into Vitae. New Wyrm's Nests and thin places may be created or destroyed at will.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Invocation </b></span></span>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> The stats of an epehemral can now be completely altered and re-arranged. Ephemerals may be destroyed or even created (with the same rules and drawbacks of embracing a mortal applying). Area of Effect can now affect mortals and other supernaturals with any of the Theme's possible uses (including opening their Third Eyes to the presence of ephemerals or the outlines of other realms around them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}